.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt PAMAUTH 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pamauth
.Nd PAM password checks for the ChatServer XMPP service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lets users sign in to ChatServer, the jabberd2 XMPP server, with their
system account.
The c2s component starts it when
.Pa c2s.xml
selects the
.Dq pipe
authreg module with
.Nm
as its program, and sends it one request per line on standard input:
.Bl -tag -width "CHECK-PASSWORD user password realm"
.It Li USER-EXISTS Ar user realm
Answers
.Li OK
if
.Xr getpwnam 3
finds
.Ar user
and the account may use chat (see below), otherwise
.Li NO .
.It Li CHECK-PASSWORD Ar user password realm
Checks the base64-encoded
.Ar password
with the
.Xr pam 3
service
.Dq jabberd ,
running both its auth and account parts.
Answers
.Li OK
or
.Li NO .
.It Li FREE
Exits.
.El
.Pp
The realm is ignored.
A request that is malformed or too long is answered with
.Li NO .
.Pp
Only accounts with a user ID of 1000 or more may use chat.
For root and the system accounts below 1000, both requests are answered
.Li NO
without asking PAM, so the chat service cannot be used to guess their
passwords.
The limit is fixed when
.Nm
is built
.Pq Dv MIN_UID .
.Pp
Results are logged to
.Xr syslog 3
with the auth facility.
.Pp
.Xr pam_unix 8
can only check passwords as root, so
.Nm
is installed setuid root and can be run only by the
.Dq jabber
group, which lets c2s itself run without privileges.
It does not delay its answer after a wrong password, because c2s waits
for it; c2s closes a stream after three failed attempts and limits the
connections per address instead.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/etc/pam.d/jabberd -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/pam.d/jabberd
The PAM policy.
As installed, its account part uses
.Xr pam_group 8
to let only the members of the
.Dq chat
group sign in.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jabber_autobuddy 8 ,
.Xr pam.conf 5 ,
.Xr pam_group 8 ,
.Xr pam_unix 8
.Sh HISTORY
Apple's ChatServer, the jabberd2 build in OS X Server, checked passwords
against Open Directory.
.Nm
replaces that for the FreeBSD port.
